    "rationale": "A: metformin (1000-1500 mg daily added to sitagliptin, Japanese type 2 diabetes patients, 24 weeks) significantly reduced LDL-cholesterol. B: no significant change in LDL-cholesterol with metformin in overweight/obese women with PCOS over up to 6 months. Exposure, outcome and within-group comparison match; one reports an effect and the other does not confirm it. The extraction gaps do not change either finding: neither extraction names the metformin arm in the group fields, A's dose field is empty although the abstract gives 1000-1500 mg daily, and B omits the metformin group size (19 cases). Abstract A does not make explicit whether the LDL reduction was tested against baseline or against ipragliflozin; the within-group reading was accepted."
